      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T15:43:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi John. Thanks for your comment.\nI\u0027m a little confused because AFAIK the backdrop-filters actually can NOT be done with RenderNodes.\nThat\u0027s right RenderNode and `Canvas#saveLayer` are all designed to focus on a *new* layer of content and RenderNode is better for this.\n\nBut `Canvas#saveLayer` can do more with the *previous* content. I\u0027m talking about the third and fourth parameters in SkCanvas::SaveLayerRec. And this is the key to filter a *backdrop* content, not *current* content.",
      "parentUuid": "edae0fd4_e7ddd89a",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f852102_3d40a321",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1392279
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T15:47:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be more specified, I found a similar solution here in flutter/engine.\nhttps://github.com/flutter/engine/blob/HEAD/flow/layers/backdrop_filter_layer.cc#L59\n\nThe Flutter team are using `SkCanvas::SaveLayerRec` to do nearly the same thing. The difference is they are using the `SkImageFilter* backdrop` param and I\u0027m using the `saveLayerFlags` to get previous (aka backdrop) content.",
      "parentUuid": "92e83218_a5677b7d",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "856ad285_c913e81b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T16:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh I missed that this is also doing the saveLayer that initializes to the existing content. We are definitely not going to re-expose that on saveLayer. It\u0027s very, very slow, which is why that capability was removed in the first place. It also can be flaky, since the content is different depending on whether or not the View or one of its ancestors is already on a layer.\n\nWe are interested in addressing the use case of \"I want to blur behind my View\", but only when we have a solution that has both adequate performance \u0026 consistent behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "1f852102_3d40a321",
      "revId": "c1db6d44ff43b9c9cc754b77592fbd769ae46917",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
